                <pb facs="0345" n="280" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg280"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/4949: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister Resident
                        in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-14T18:00:00-04:00">August 14, 1936—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>338. Department’s 337, August 13, 5 p.m. A further telegram from the Paris
                    Embassy states that the French Foreign Office has suggested that you take up
                    with the Italian high command the question of avoiding any difficulty regarding
                    the importation of the shipment into Ethiopia.</p>
                <p>If any objections are raised by the Italian authorities please report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
